<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:49Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Iran signals satisfaction, skepticism after US midterm vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5556dff3f9d34f7fe8dc0dc05a0a69407a3e1a6d09d5f637d933f56961048db8</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149--f14e22022dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the Iranian regime says the US midterms will not change Washington's policy toward Tehran, some officials and commentators see the resounding Democratic victory as blowback against the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Trump's midterm elections loss mean for strained US-India ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9c03ebcc1c005e32444b9bff7219cfaf84245b0c138656eafcbc4a0814d34d3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777--7836c1679b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's electoral setback might give New Delhi and Washington space to reset relations, but there is no guarantee that the US will actually change its approach to India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea tells EU to 'mind its own business' on human rights</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d614cfeec773785b1856efe3c898df88316ba96ac63924c3244030a115da5430</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196--b096a2c3122f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-tells-eu-to-mind-its-own-business-on-human-rights/a-79862196?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's UN mission has lashed out at the European Union over a draft UN resolution. Pyongyang has said the West does not have a monopoly on human rights.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Several European flights receive bomb threats, some divert</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3fe3a619e4a2dde23fcdaf26753d0dec4dbae19eaf5a6514c29102d4ac546039</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T10:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/several-european-flights-receive-bomb-threats-some-divert/a-79861216--778bd07a8276.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/several-european-flights-receive-bomb-threats-some-divert/a-79861216?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At least a dozen flights were either diverted or landed with a military escort after bomb or security threats. The first reported case involved a flight from Dublin to Rome landing outside Paris and more soon followed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:96586c7d7d54ca8b808f8f6cd72ae3500a2c3452a803eebc5113303f3e5cd5e0</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:35:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5640416cff9f93bcd577b722d2e4e67bb0b366a4c0fb6787979a88bfcde57d84</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T07:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Winners, losers, the EU: Five takeaways from the US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d865116738006cec3dde0a29e8b055821a264208acd9b8dcec1a6a524a8d84e9</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901--d5d91689d3d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans suffered a crushing defeat in Tuesday's midterm elections, with the Democrats wresting control of Congress. What does this mean for US politics and the world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>36 years later: Hungary opens Communist-era secret service files</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e8a785a7231840003eb7e8e0bc595db2b3ddf809687bb38690cf5aae3ba2d81</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016--dc09772faa12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Decades after the end of Soviet rule, Hungary is releasing all its secret service files. The disclosure is sparking fresh debate about informants, guilt and responsibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo: Outrage as authorities accused of not helping femicide victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f31df5d13fac73cbe5f0a4c4efedc4c63dcabed0f051665f845d29576a3cefd</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726--34859fc77a44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's shifting role in the global drug trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:083d4eebf0d9af2d32c19688ca4659bfa59478fb264bf0d6495fd4a1938ab73e</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720--a33472b9e48a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent discoveries of meth labs suggest parts of Africa are moving beyond drug transit and becoming sites of synthetic drug production.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9748c49568d5d173753da607ddffb23df6aa9e23c47fc879269b026a7f3e0bf6</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wawira Njiru, Kenya's school feeder and German Africa Prize recipient</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d1fcdcd8aa45a62a52e70fbffb70c3cb51c4d6acfe9897fea26cf2f858eb1c3</id><updated>2026-11-05T16:34:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537--47b719bb31e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wawira-njiru-kenya-s-school-feeder-and-german-africa-prize-recipient/a-79646537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Standing ovations in Berlin: Kenyan social entrepreneur Wawira Njiru received the German Africa Award for her school feeding programme, which now provides meals to 730,000 children every day.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
